## Purpose

The rules that apply **while working on {{project}}** — and nowhere else. They live in their own
file so that a block, or a different project cloned from the same engine, does not inherit them.

> ⛔ **`bin/init` does not fill this file's rules in.** It generates the shape; the rules are
> **criterion**, and the AI does not invent criterion (`ADR-003`). Every ⬜ below is a question
> for {{owner}}, and an unanswered one is an honest gap — not a blank to guess at.

---

## 0 · THE THREE LEVELS — where this file sits

```
🌐 UNIVERSAL   Mente/base-rules.md        any project, any block, from the first response
      │ inherits (may ADD or TIGHTEN — never LOOSEN)
      ▼
🏢 PROJECT     PROJECT-RULES.md  ← YOU ARE HERE
      │ inherits
      ▼
📦 BLOCK       Mente/blocks/active/<name>/BLOCK.md §B
```

⛔ **A lower level can never grant itself what a higher level forbids.** Exceptions are
{{owner}}'s only, and become a **new rule at the parent's level** with its own ADR.

