## 3 · 🌉 THE GATE — other Mente OS instances

If another project has its own Mente OS, this one **points at it but does not integrate it** —
integrating burns tokens with no request behind it. Declare each gate in `mente.config.yml`
(`gates:`), which is what the harness reads.

| | |
|---|---|
| ⛔ **Never read** | ⬜ path — see `mente.config.yml` `gates:` |
| **Open** | `acceder mente <project>` → confirm the WHY → **read-only + report** |
| **Close** | `cerrar mente <project>`, or auto-close when the task ends |
| **Enforcement** | 🔒 `deny` on Read/Edit/Write in **both** settings files |

⭐ **A gate is a technical lock, not a promise.** In this project's own history it was doctrine
for one session and got violated 6 times. **Never propose lifting a `deny` for convenience.**

